From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 23:38:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_servers: add per-agent acp_flavor setting to force
 subagent grouping

The subagent-grouping adapter was auto-selected from the agent's self-reported
name, which differs across environments. Add an `acp_flavor` setting on each
agent under `agent_servers` ("auto" | "qwen" | "none"; default auto). An explicit
value forces or disables qwen-style grouping; "auto" keeps the name-based
detection. Threaded settings_content::AcpFlavor -> project (From + accessor) ->
custom::connect -> AcpConnection::stdio, where it overrides the name match.

Verified: cargo check --workspace exit 0; cargo test -p acp_thread 76 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
