 - `NativeAgentConnection` returns `NativeSubagentGrouping`.
 - `AcpConnection` (`crates/agent_servers/src/acp.rs`) returns an adapter chosen from the
-  agent's reported `agentInfo.name` (e.g. `"qwen-code"` → `QwenSubagentGrouping`).
+  per-agent `acp_flavor` setting, falling back to the agent's reported `agentInfo.name`.
 - Unknown providers → `None` → today's flat behavior, **zero regression**.
 
+### Manual flavor override (`acp_flavor` setting)
+
+Because an agent's self-reported name varies across environments, each agent under
+`agent_servers` in settings takes an optional `acp_flavor`:
+
+```json
+"agent_servers": {
+  "my-qwen-thing": {
+    "command": { "path": "qwen", "args": ["--acp"] },
+    "acp_flavor": "qwen"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Values: `auto` (default — detect from the reported name), `qwen` (force qwen grouping),
+`none` (disable grouping). Defined as `settings_content::AcpFlavor`, carried through
+`project::CustomAgentServerSettings::acp_flavor()` and `agent_servers::custom::connect`
+into `AcpConnection::stdio`, where it overrides the name-based selection.
+
 This trait + the `subagent_grouping()` connection method is the concrete "extension point
 for ACP providers" the exploration set out to find.
 
